  "id": "phase-locking",
  "term": "phase locking",
  "definition": "Phase locking is the degree to which the phases of neural oscillations stay consistently aligned over time. In plain terms, it describes how regularly the timing of rhythmic brain activity matches up, which can support more effective information flow between neural networks.",
